"win.help.quickStart.step1.title" = "Optional: restart as administrator";
"win.help.quickStart.step1.body" = "As a standard user, some system folders are skipped. Administrator rights give complete results; everything else works either way.";
"win.help.quickStart.step2.title" = "Click “Scan All”";
"win.help.quickStart.step2.body" = "Internal drives are scanned right away. If USB drives or memory cards are connected, the app asks which ones to include. You can cancel at any time.";
"win.help.quickStart.step3.title" = "Read the Summary";
"win.help.quickStart.step3.body" = "Findings are sorted by severity: Critical, Warning, Tip. Click “Show” to jump to the folder, Docker or duplicate list behind each one.";
"win.help.quickStart.step4.title" = "Clean up safely";
"win.help.quickStart.step4.body" = "Removed items go to the Recycle Bin and can be restored. Windows, Program Files, your profile folders and drive roots are locked.";
"win.help.admin.title" = "Administrator rights";
"win.help.admin.body" = "Windows protects some folders (Windows, other users’ profiles, System Volume Information). A standard user cannot list them, so they are skipped and the total looks smaller.\n\nClick “Restart as administrator” and accept the Windows prompt. The app reopens with full access. It only reads file names and sizes — nothing is uploaded anywhere.";
"win.help.scanning.title" = "Scanning drives";
"win.help.scanning.body" = "“Scan All” scans the Windows drive and other internal drives. USB drives, external SSDs and memory cards are listed first and only scanned after you confirm — tick the ones you want. “Remember my choice” skips the question next time (change it in Settings).\n\nWhen you plug in a drive while the app is open, it offers to scan it.\n\nSizes are the space actually used on disk (“Size on disk”). Hard links (common in Windows\\WinSxS) are counted once, and junctions, symbolic links and mounted folders are never followed, so totals are not inflated.";
"win.help.folders.body" = "Open a drive and choose “Folders”. The list is sorted largest first; the treemap shows the same items as rectangles sized by space.\n\nDouble-click a folder to open it and use the path at the top to go back. Select items (Ctrl/Shift for several), then use Show in Explorer, Open or Move to Recycle Bin.\n\n“Categories” shows space by purpose (apps, photos, developer files, caches…). “Large Files” lists the biggest files on the drive.";
"win.help.docker.title" = "Cleaning Docker";
"win.help.docker.body" = "The Docker page works step by step:\n1. Is Docker installed? If not, nothing else happens and no command is run.\n2. Is Docker running? If not, start Docker Desktop and click “Check again”.\n3. List images tagged <none> (dangling) — leftovers from rebuilding images that no container uses.\n4. Remove the ones you select, after confirmation.\n\nImages are removed without --force, so Docker refuses to remove anything still used by a container.\n\nDocker Desktop keeps everything in a WSL 2 virtual disk (.vhdx). It does not shrink automatically after cleaning.";
"win.help.deleting.title" = "Deleting & restoring";
"win.help.deleting.body" = "Clean My Mac sends files to the Recycle Bin. To restore, open the Recycle Bin, right-click the file and choose “Restore”.\n\nUSB sticks and memory cards have no Recycle Bin. For items there the app warns you clearly and asks before deleting permanently.\n\nWindows, Program Files, ProgramData, your profile folders (Desktop, Documents, Downloads, AppData), the root of each drive and the app itself are locked.\n\nThe Deletion Log lists everything removed by the app. Space is freed for good after you empty the Recycle Bin.";
"win.help.faq.title" = "FAQ";
"win.help.faq.body" = "Why does the total differ from the drive’s used space?\nWindows also counts restore points, NTFS metadata and folders a standard user cannot read. They are shown as “System data & unreadable”.\n\nWindows SmartScreen warns about the installer.\nThe build is not signed with a commercial certificate. Click “More info” › “Run anyway”.\n\nWhich Windows versions are supported?\nWindows 10 version 1809 and later, and Windows 11, on x64 and ARM64 PCs.\n\nDoes the app use the network?\nNo.";
